# UI Test Queries

Challenge UI tests must stay implementation-flexible. Do not require a specific label/`htmlFor`/`aria-labelledby` wiring pattern.

## Query priority

1. **Accessible roles** — `getByRole` / `findByRole` with an accessible name
2. **`data-testid`** — only when there is no stable role (e.g. summary tiles, list field tiles)

```tsx
// ✅ Preferred
screen.getByRole("combobox", { name: /status filter/i });
screen.getByRole("button", { name: /claim brief/i });

// ✅ OK when no role fits
screen.getByTestId("summary-open");

// ❌ Avoid — couples tests to one labeling style
screen.getByLabelText("Status filter");
```

## Authoring implications

- Name controls for assistive tech somehow (`aria-label` **or** associated `<label>`).
- Prefer stable accessible names in task copy so exercise UIs need not copy solution markup.
- Task titles must name exactly what the test asserts — one behavior per task.
- **Basic before conflict:** for the same control, add happy-path before 409 / race / stale-response tests.
- **Form save is product:** if the UI has Edit → draft fields → Save, include a test that asserts the PATCH/PUT **request body** uses draft values **and** the UI reflects notes/status/version after success. A 409-only save test is not enough (false green).
- Do not add `data-testid` for ordinary buttons/inputs/selects that already have roles.
- Use `data-testid` for non-interactive display fields when free-text matching would couple to copy.
